.TH "AG\-CLI\-AUTH\-LOGIN" "1" "2026\-10\-09" "AtomGit CLI 0.7.4" "AtomGit CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
\&ag\-cli\-auth\-login \- Log in with AtomGit OAuth (opens browser, saves token.json)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\&ag\-cli auth login [flags]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
\&Opens a browser to authorize ag\-cli against atomgit.com, then writes
\&access_token and user to the XDG config path (see README). With \-\-with\-token,
\&skips the browser and reads an existing access token (PAT or OAuth token)
\&from standard input instead — useful in sandboxes, containers, and CI where
\&no browser is available:
.PP
\&    echo \(dq$TOKEN\(dq | ag\-cli auth login \-\-with\-token
\&    ag\-cli auth login \-\-with\-token < token.txt
.PP
\&Piped or redirected input is read to EOF without any prompt; in an
\&interactive terminal a single hidden prompt is shown. The token is validated
\&against the AtomGit user API before it is saved. If already logged in, skips
\&unless \-\-force is set. The first saved account becomes active; later logins
\&do not change the active account.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
\&Always authenticate again even if already logged in
\&Default: \(dqfalse\(dq.
.TP
\fB\-\-git\-email <string>\fR
\&Override the Git user.email stored for this account
\&Default: \(dq\(dq.
.TP
\fB\-\-git\-name <string>\fR
\&Override the Git user.name stored for this account
\&Default: \(dq\(dq.
.TP
\fB\-\-with\-token\fR
\&Read an access token from standard input instead of browser OAuth
\&Default: \(dqfalse\(dq.
.SH INHERITED OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
\&Show help for command
\&Default: \(dqfalse\(dq.
.TP
\fB\-\-raw\-output\fR
\&Disable terminal output sanitization for machine processing
\&Default: \(dqfalse\(dq.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBag\-cli\-auth\fR(1)
